---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="About ExpatWon"
  description="ExpatWon is written by Michael Han — a Korean manufacturing-company CEO since 2016, ISO lead auditor, and expat executive living both sides of the desk."
>
  <article class="prose-article mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <img
      src="/logo-full.svg"
      alt="ExpatWon — Money & Life in Korea"
      width="980"
      height="320"
      class="mx-auto mb-10 w-full max-w-md"
    />
    <h1 class="mb-4 font-display text-4xl font-bold text-ink">About ExpatWon</h1>

    <p>
      ExpatWon exists because most information about money in Korea is written
      in Korean, for Koreans — and most English information is either outdated
      or copied from other blogs by people who never actually did the thing
      they are describing.
    </p>

    <h2 id="author">Who writes this</h2>

    <div class="my-6 flex flex-col items-center gap-5 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/60 p-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-start">
      <picture class="flex-none">
        <source srcset="/author.webp" type="image/webp" />
        <img
          src="/author.jpg"
          alt="Michael Han — founder and CEO of Danji Co., Ltd."
          width="320"
          height="320"
          class="h-28 w-28 rounded-full object-cover ring-1 ring-slate-200"
        />
      </picture>
      <div class="text-center sm:text-left">
        <p class="my-0 font-display text-2xl font-bold text-ink">Michael Han</p>
        <p class="my-1 text-[0.8rem] font-semibold tracking-wider text-slate-400 uppercase">
          Founder &amp; CEO, Danji Co., Ltd. · MD, VSL Vietnam
        </p>
        <p class="my-0 text-[0.95rem] leading-relaxed text-slate-500">
          Ten years running a Korean company — and now a foreigner building one
          abroad. Both sides of the desk this site writes about.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      ExpatWon is written by <strong>Michael Han</strong> — founder
      and CEO of <strong>Danji Co., Ltd. (주식회사 단지)</strong>, a Korean
      food-manufacturing company he has operated since March 2016, and, since
      April 2025, Managing Director of <strong>VSL Vietnam</strong> in Hanoi.
    </p>
    <p>
      That combination is the point of this site. As a Korean company owner,
      he has spent a decade on the operator's side of the systems covered
      here — corporate and personal banking, loan reviews, payroll and the
      four social insurances, company vehicles and their tax caps, business
      registration, food-safety compliance. And as an executive building a
      company abroad, he lives the expat side too: work permits, foreign
      KYC, and being the customer the local system was not designed for.
    </p>
    <p>
      He is a certified lead auditor for <strong>ISO 9001:2015</strong>
      (quality), <strong>ISO 14001:2015</strong> (environmental) and
      <strong>ISO 45001:2018</strong> (occupational health &amp; safety)
      management systems (Korea Enterprise Certification Inc., 2025). The
      audit habit carries over to the writing: claims need documents, which
      is why every figure on this site links to the institution that
      publishes it.
    </p>

    <h2>How we work</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Official sources only.</strong> Every figure links to the
        institution that publishes it: the Financial Supervisory Service, the
        National Tax Service, Korea Immigration Service, the National Health
        Insurance Service, or the banks' own English pages.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>How it works, not what to buy.</strong> We explain processes
        and costs. Where we use affiliate links, they are disclosed on the
        page and never change what we write.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Dated and verified.</strong> Every article shows when it was
        last verified. Korean regulations change often; if you spot something
        outdated, <a href="/contact/">tell us</a> and we will fix it.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>What ExpatWon is not</h2>
    <p>
      We are not a bank, a lender, an insurer, or a licensed advisor. Nothing
      here is financial, legal, or tax advice — see the
      <a href="/disclaimer/">disclaimer</a>. For decisions with real money at
      stake, confirm the current rules with the official source or a licensed
      professional.
    </p>
  </article>
</Layout>
